Scenario: A parent spawns a child before the selected environment is configured. The child sees it starting, waits, and receives the ready result after an ordinary parent turn-settings update.

## Window 1
-- request 1 (request; parent delegates while the environment is starting) --
00:message/developer:
    <MODEL_INSTRUCTIONS>
01:message/developer[2]:
    [01] <PERMISSIONS_INSTRUCTIONS>
    [02] <ENVIRONMENTS_INSTRUCTIONS>
02:message/developer:
    <MULTI_AGENT_ROLE>
03:message/developer:
    <MULTI_AGENT_MODE>
04:message/user:
    <ENVIRONMENT_CONTEXT>
05:message/user:
    Delegate waiting for the shared workspace, and report what the worker finds.
-- request 2 (request; parent waits for the worker) --
06:function_call/agentroute_collaboration.spawn_agent:{"fork_turns":"none","message":"Wait for the shared workspace to become ready.","task_name":"worker"}
07:function_call_output:{"task_name":"/root/worker"}

